      'SGA 4 Exposé X (M. Artin, « Dimension cohomologique : premiers résultats »), read in the retyped edition of SGA 4 (normalesup.org/~forgogozo/SGA4/10/10.pdf), whose numbering follows the original: Corollaire 2.4 — A noetherian local with residue field k, ℓ invertible in A, and ℓ ≠ 2 or no residue field of Spec A orderable: cd_ℓ R(A) ≥ cd_ℓ k + dim A, proved by induction on dim A down to the henselian dimension-1 case (Théorème 2.3: cd_ℓ R(A) ≤ cd_ℓ k + 1, with equality if ℓ ≠ 2 or k is not orderable). The example after 2.3 is the page’s marginal one: the henselisation at the origin of ℝ[x, y]/(x² + y²), where equality fails for ℓ = 2. Corollaire 2.5: cd_ℓ R(X) ≥ dim X. Nothing there on the finer exception (an orderable k(x) with cd₂ k(x)(√−1) finite), on the catenary and universally japanese refinement to « k real », nor on the regular case.',
