    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder16.lean', found: "Partly: the grading projectors lie in ℰ, over ℤ and with no module; Λ and the primitive projectors are not proved. Added 2026-10-25: Holds, over ℤ and with no module: in a ring E graded by orthogonal idempotents π_a, a subring ℰ containing L of degree 2 and one-sided inverses w_i of L^{n−i} ((6.3)) contains every grading projector, every projector p_{j,β} of the primitive decomposition (read in E as orthogonal idempotents onto L^β P^j, commuting with L block by block and with image in L^β p_{j,0} E), and the pseudo-inverse Λ = Σ L^β w_j L^{n−j−β−1} p_{j,β+1}, which has degree −2 and satisfies (6.7), LΛ = 1 − Σ p_{j,0} and ΛL = 1 − Σ p_{j,n−j}. Everything rests on one block identity, L^β w_j L^{n−j−β} p_{j,β} = p_{j,β}; once the π_a are known, the folder's double descending induction reduces to a single induction on the primitive degree, through (6.9) below the middle and (6.10) above it. The reading's displayed formula for Λ on a bottom block, Λπ_{i,α} = w_{i−2α}L^{n−i+α}π_{i,α}, has degree −2α: it lacks a factor L^{α−1} and is right only for α = 1; the top-block formula is right. Not formalised: the existence of the primitive decomposition from (6.3), which the folder takes as known; the converses (2) ⇒ (1) and (3) ⇒ (1) of the theorem of p. 9; the Remarque's characterisation in L and Λ alone. Added 2026-10-25: The converse (3) ⇒ (1) of the theorem of p. 9 holds only for the projectors: if every primitive projector p_{j,β} lies in ℰ, so does every grading projector π_a, since π_a is the sum of the blocks p_{j,β} with j + 2β = a (projecteurs_mem_of_primitifs). The rest is false, and Lean proves the counterexample (reciproque_trois_un_fausse): in E = M₂(R), R any nonzero commutative ring (ℤ or a field), n = 1, L = e₂₁, the primitive decomposition and the inverse e₁₂ of L exist in E, and the subring ℰ of lower-triangular matrices contains L, every π_a and every p_{j,β}, yet no w ∈ ℰ satisfies w L π₀ = π₀ and no Λ ∈ ℰ satisfies LΛ = 1 − Σ p_{j,0}. So (3) implies neither (1) nor (2): the projectors say nothing about the elements of negative degree in ℰ. Still not formalised: the existence of the primitive decomposition from (6.3); the converse (2) ⇒ (1); the Remarque's characterisation in L and Λ alone." },
