    settle:
      "Searched 2026-10-25 with WebSearch (several queries in English and French on anti-affine group schemes over a base, affinisation of group schemes over a DVR/mixed characteristic, constructibility of G_aff), the Stack Exchange API on MathOverflow ('anti-affine', 'affinization group scheme', 'universal vector extension anti-affine': nothing relevant), and full text of SGA 3 exposé VI_B (Polo's edition, §§11–13 read) and of arXiv:0710.5211, 1509.03059, 1101.2771, 2101.10829 (grepped for constructibility, families, base rings, DVRs, specialisation). Found: the field-level dichotomy (characteristic 0 vs p) is classical (Rosenlicht 1958, Brion 2009); SGA 3 VI_B §12 (Raynaud, Gabber) treats G_af over a regular base of dimension <= 1 but says nothing about the fibrewise variation of (G_s)_aff; Brion (2009, 2017) explicitly leaves the theory over DVRs open. No printed statement that s -> (G_s)_aff is not constructible, nor the mixed-characteristic example. Remains: Raynaud, Faisceaux amples (LNM 119, 1970), ch. VII §3, not accessible online here and not read; Sancho de Salas' work on anti-affine groups (Sa01, SS09) not checked for a relative version; the page's equal-characteristic constructibility assertion was not looked up. Closest in print: SGA 3, exp. VI_B, Prop. 12.10 and Rem. 12.8/12.10.2 (Raynaud, Gabber; editors' addition to the 2011 edition): over a DVR, G -> G_af is faithfully flat and A(G_af)/π injects into A(G_s); Gabber's examples with abelian generic fibre and non-smooth kernel. These concern the existence and flatness of the relative affine quotient, not the failure of constructibility of the fibrewise (G_s)_aff, and give no extension of an abelian scheme by G_a with (G_y)_aff = 1 in characteristic 0 and (G_s)_aff = G_a in characteristic p. The field-level ingredient (char 0 vs char p behaviour of extensions of abelian varieties by vector groups) is printed in Rosenlicht 1958 and Brion 2009.",
