    claim:
      'The folder asserts, without proof, that a topos glued from an open subtopos X₀ and its closed complement X₁ along a left exact φ : F(X₀) → F(X₁) is a presheaf topos Top(X) exactly when X₀ and X₁ are presheaf topoi Top(X₀), Top(X₁) and φ commutes with all projective limits, the gluing datum then being a bifunctor h : X₀^op × X₁ → (Ens).',
    basis:
      'Pages 6–7 write « Un cas particulièrement important pour nous est celui où X est de la forme Top(X), [illegible] X dans (Cat), il revient au même de dire que » X₀, X₁ are of the form Top(X₀), Top(X₁) and that φ commutes with arbitrary projective limits, i.e. has a left adjoint f^*, defined by a functor X₁ → X̂₀ extended by continuity in inductive limits, « correspondant i.e. à un bifoncteur » (x₀, x₁) ↦ h(x₁, x₀). « Top(X) » is written over a struck illegible word, « Top(X₀), Top(X₁) » over a struck « X̂₀, X̂₁ »; the words before « X dans (Cat) », before « un adjoint à g. » and at the start of the parenthesis on continuity are illegible. None of them carries the equivalence.',
    ours:
      'Every step of the proof is the reading’s, footnoted as its own: a subterminal of a presheaf topos is a sieve, cutting X into the full sieve X₀ and the cosieve X₁; the gluing functor is then restriction of a right Kan extension, hence continuous, and h(x₁, x₀) = Hom_X(x₀, x₁); conversely any h defines a category — the collage, or cograph, of the profunctor h — whose presheaf topos is the gluing. The reading sets this out as a forward statement followed by « Réciproquement »; this pass reads the page’s « il revient au même » as an equivalence and checks both halves. From memory, the direction from a profunctor to a gluing is standard; if anything here is a candidate it is the necessity half — a gluing that is a presheaf topos has a continuous gluing functor — which follows in two lines from subterminals of presheaf topoi being sieves and is likely folklore. Written on Opus 5.5 against a reading made on Opus 5.',
    literature: [
      "A. Grothendieck and J.-L. Verdier, « Topos », SGA 4, exposé IV, in Théorie des topos et cohomologie étale des schémas I, Lecture Notes in Math. 269, Springer, 1972 (séminaire 1963/64) — Exercice 9.5.10 « Recollement de topos de la forme Ĉ », original pp. 470–471 (pp. 283–284 of the retyped edition, read 2026-10-25 from matematicas.unex.es/~navarro/res/sga/) — a) the open subtopoi of E = Ĉ correspond to the sieves C' of C, with E/U ≃ Ĉ' and closed complement F ≃ Ĉ'' for C'' the complementary full subcategory; b) the bifunctor h : C'^op × C'' → (Ens), h(X', X'') = Hom_C(X', X'') (9.5.10.1), reconstructs C from C', C'' and h, h being arbitrary, and h amounts to a continuous σ : Ĉ'' → Ĉ' (9.5.10.2) whose right adjoint ρ : Ĉ' → Ĉ'' (9.5.10.3) is the gluing functor of the open subtopos Ĉ'; c) for a gluing functor ρ between two presheaf categories, the glued topos E is equivalent to some Ĉ iff ρ commutes with small products (i.e. has a left adjoint 9.5.10.2) iff i : Ĉ'' → E is essential, and C is then made explicit from the bifunctor h; d) gluing two point topoi need not give a presheaf topos. Both halves of the finding, with the same bifunctor h(x₁, x₀) = Hom_X(x₀, x₁).",
      "Same, Exercice 9.5.9 a), original p. 470 (retyped p. 282–283) — i_* commutes with products iff ρ does iff ρ has a left adjoint σ = j^* i_!, these ρ corresponding to continuous σ : F → U; the general fact used in 9.5.10 c).",
    ],
    status: 'matched',
    settle:
      "Searched 2026-10-25 with WebSearch and curl (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5), following the settle field's first suggestion: downloaded the retyped SGA 4 tome I (matematicas.unex.es copy, 332 pp.), extracted text with pdftotext and read exposé IV, exercises 9.5.9–9.5.10 in full. Exercise 9.5.10 states the finding: sieves of C give the open subtopoi of Ĉ with closed complement the presheaf topos on the complementary full subcategory, the gluing is recovered from the bifunctor h(X', X'') = Hom_C(X', X''), h arbitrary, and for a gluing of two presheaf topoi, E ≃ Ĉ iff the gluing functor commutes with small products (has a left adjoint). This confirms, now read, the citation the modernised reading 116 already gives at p. 7 (issue #59). Not consulted: Johnstone's Elephant A2.1/A4.5, Wraith 1974, Carboni–Johnstone 1995, nLab — unnecessary for the match since SGA 4 (1972, seminar 1963/64) is earlier. The leaves are dated by the inventory « [à partir de 1981] »; no priority question arises. Remaining: nothing on the literature side; the entry can be marked matched.",
