    lean: { file: "lean/Grothendieck/Folder136.lean", found: "Partly: the step page 8 asserts without proof — each row of fixed total degree is exact — holds on every simplex, over any commutative ring k, in the coordinate model C^{••}_{[m]} ≅ k{T}{Y_1, …, Y_m}[dY_1, …, dY_m] (dT = 0) that pages 5–7 give, with any finite linearly ordered set of variables. The proof is an explicit contracting homotopy with no division: at the least variable j a monomial involves, H(Y^{(β)} dY_I) = Y^{(β+e_j)} dY_{I∖j} if j ∈ I and 0 otherwise, and Hd + dH = 1 − P with P the projection on the constants T^{(a)} (pdH_pdD_add) — the tensor-product homotopy of the one-variable complexes, made integral by the divided powers where the Euler homotopy divides by the weight. Hence in total degree n every cocycle of exterior degree q ≥ 1 is a coboundary (exact_of_pos), the cocycles of exterior degree 0 are the c T^{(n)} with c unique (cocycle_zero, smul_tPow_eq_zero), and T^{(j)} acts by c_{j,n} (pdD_tMul, tMul_tMul, tMul_tPow): graded by total degree the cohomology of Δ[m] is k{T} = τ_{≥0}(H^0 ⊗ k{T}), the statement for X = Δ[m] (pd_row_cohomology). Not formalised: the identification of the model with Γ^pΦ ⊗ Λ^qΨ and its simplicial structure, the acyclicity of C^{p,q}_* for p ≥ 1 (Proposition 1, Φ_* ≃ 0), and the passage to an arbitrary simplicial set X, which needs the cohomology of simplicial sets with coefficients in simplicial modules." },
