      "J. Kollár, Families of varieties of general type, Cambridge Tracts in Math. 231 (2023), author's final version modbook-final.pdf, searched in full text. Theorem 10.72 (p. 403) is the strengthening of Hironaka: (s,S) normal, local and excellent, X S_2, f of finite type and pure relative dimension n, pure(X_s) geometrically normal (or seminormal and S_2); then f is flat with normal fibres. Theorem 3.9 (p. 130) says the Hilbert-to-Chow map is a local isomorphism over geometrically normal projective subvarieties, on the seminormalization; §3.14 restricts Cayley-Chow theory to seminormal bases. Claim 2.71.1: with pure-dimensional fibres, pure relative dimension is the same as universally open.",
      'Web search, 10 October 2026: « universally open morphism reduced base fibre generically reduced normal reduction implies flat normal Hironaka lemma », then « Kollár "Simultaneous normalization and algebra husks" Hironaka ». The abstract of Kollár, « Simultaneous normalization and algebra husks » (Asian J. Math. 15, 2011; arXiv 0910.1076), attributes to Hironaka the case S regular: fibres generically reduced with normal reductions ⇒ red X → S flat with normal fibres. The paper itself was not read.',
