    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder5.lean', found: "Only the arithmetic of the coefficients, the reachable piece: qᵢ = (p^{i+1})!/((p^i)!)^p satisfies ((p^i)!)^p · qᵢ = (p^{i+1})!, so it is an integer, the multinomial coefficient of p blocks of size p^i (factorial_eq_mul_q, q_eq_multinomial), for every p; for p prime, (p − 1)v_p((p^i)!) = p^i − 1 and v_p(qᵢ) = 1 (padicValNat_q), by Legendre in the form v_p((pm)!) = v_p(m!) + m, which confirms the value the pass's remark on the reading's footnote uses. In any ring with a divided-power ideal, γ_{p^i}(x)^p = qᵢ γ_{p^{i+1}}(x) (dpow_pow_eq_q), the relation of the presentation; it is mathlib's DividedPowers.prod_dpow specialised. Not formalised: the universality of W[Λ]/(…), the necessity half of the lemmas, the normal form in the Θᵢ, c(ν), the quotients W^{(ν,r)}, the bound of page 8. Added 2026-10-25: The universality of page 4 holds, more generally than stated: over any domain W of characteristic zero in which the integers prime to p are units (W(k), ℤ_p), W^{(ν)} = W[Λ₀, …, Λ_ν]/(Λᵢ^p − qᵢΛ_{i+1}, Λ_ν^p, Λ₀ − p) carries divided powers δ on J = (Λ₀, …, Λ_ν) with δ_{p^i}(p) = Λᵢ and δ_n = 0 on J for n ≥ p^{ν+1}, and it is initial among W-algebras with a divided-power ideal (I, γ) containing p with γ_n(p) = 0 for n ≥ p^{ν+1}; locality, artinianity and the residue field play no role (universal, dpWν, dpWν_p, dpWν_eq_zero, presentation). The proof avoids the PD envelope of the reading's footnote: Λᵢ ↦ X^{p^i}/(p^i)! embeds A^{(ν)} = W[Λ]/(Λᵢ^p − qᵢΛ_{i+1}, Λ_ν^p) in K[X]/(X^{p^{ν+1}}), K = Frac W, because the box monomials (aᵢ < p) span by the carry of page 8 and go to distinct powers of X (psi_injective); the divided powers x^n/n! come back to (Λ) because C(k, p^e)γ_k = γ_{p^e}γ_{k−p^e} with C(k, p^e) prime to p by Lucas (dpow_split); and (Λ₀ − p) ∩ (Λ) = (Λ₀ − p)(Λ), via the augmentation, is a sub-PD ideal (isSubDPIdeal_Kp). This also settles the pass's worry about the footnote: γ_{p^{ν+1}}(p) = 0 in W^{(ν)} holds for the constructed δ, not as a consequence of the relations. The sufficiency half of the lemma of page 5 holds for any λᵢ with λ₀ = p, λᵢ^p = qᵢλ_{i+1}: p^iΘᵢ = 0 and p^νλ_ν^p = 0 in W^{(ν)}, hence p^{ν+pm} = 0 when λ_ν = p^m·unit, i.e. p^{c(ν)} = 0 (p_pow_mul_Θ_mem, p_pow_mem_Kp), without the binomial expansion. Not formalised: the necessity half (that conditions a)–b) cut out an ideal), hence the normal form in the Θᵢ, the length, the exact order p^{c(ν)} of 1, and the quotients W^{(ν,r)} of page 7. Added 2026-10-25: The necessity half of the lemma of page 5 holds, so the normal form is proved: with λ₀ = p, λᵢ^p = qᵢλ_{i+1}, λ_ν = p^m·unit and Θᵢ = Λᵢ − λᵢ, the box monomials Θ^a (0 ≤ aᵢ < p) form a basis of A^{(ν)}, and Σ w_aΘ^a ∈ (Λ₀ − p) iff p^i ∣ w_a when aᵢ is the first nonzero exponent and p^{c(ν)} ∣ w_0, c(ν) = ν + pm (normalForm, tmono_linearIndependent); hence W^{(ν)} ≅ ⊕_a W/p^{ord a} as a W-module (WνEquiv), p^k = 0 in W^{(ν)} iff k ≥ c(ν) when p is not a unit, so 1 has exact order p^{c(ν)} (p_pow_eq_zero_iff), and over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser p the length is p + p² + ⋯ + p^ν + pm, which telescopes to the reading's c(ν) + Σ_{i=1}^{ν} i(p−1)p^{ν−i} (length_Wν_eq; 4 for p = 2, ν = 1). The key step is that the span of the p^{min(ord a, n)}Θ^a is an ideal, by descending induction on the factor Θⱼ through the carry Θᵢ^p = qᵢΘ_{i+1} − Σ_{0<k<p} C(p,k)λᵢ^{p−k}Θᵢ^k, in which the constant λᵢ^p cancels for i < ν; it uses only p ∣ qᵢ. For the usual λᵢ = p^{p^i}/(p^i)! (exists_lamStd), m = p^ν − v_p((p^ν)!), and for W = ℤ_p the order of 1 and the length are as stated (padicInt_Wν). This replaces the machine check for six (p, ν) by a proof for all p and ν. Not formalised: the quotients W^{(ν,r)} of page 7." },
