    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder153.lean', found: 'Partly, for K₀ flat over k₀: the co-addition and co-multiplication of Ω exist and are unique in Ω ⊗ Ω whenever Ω is free and the map K₀ ⊗_{k₀} Ω → K₀[T], a ⊗ F ↦ aF, is injective (coaddition_existsUnique_of_injective, comultiplication_existsUnique_of_injective). That map is always surjective, since k₀[T] ⊂ Ω, and it is injective for K₀ a localisation (Ω free) and for K₀ flat over k₀ with K₀ ⊗_{k₀} K₀ = K₀ (omegaBaseChange_injective_of_flat). Neither the inclusion k₀ ⊂ K₀ nor the identification K₀[X] ⊗ K₀[Y] = K₀[X, Y] is used. Not proved: injectivity, hence the co-operations, from K₀ ⊗ K₀ = K₀ and Ω free alone, without flatness; plethory axioms beyond the co-operations.' },
