      'D. Edidin, Z. Hu, « The integral Chow rings of the stacks of hyperelliptic Weierstrass points », Michigan Math. J. (2025), doi:10.1307/mmj/20236479, arXiv:2208.00556 — read 2026-10-25: their § 3 presents [M_{0,2g+2}/𝔖_{2g+1}] as a twisted ℙ¹ with an étale divisor of degree 2g + 2 and one section of it, i.e. binary forms with one marked root; Theorem 1.3 (g ≥ 2): A*([M_{0,2g+2}/𝔖_{2g+1}]) = ℤ[l]/(2g(2g + 1) l), so Pic is cyclic of order (n − 1)(n − 2) for n = 2g + 2 ≥ 6 (20 for n = 6), and A*(H_{g,w}) = ℤ[ψ]/(4g(2g + 1) ψ). The generator is given in torus coordinates, not as the tangent line; since L_n has order (n − 1)(n − 2) in a cyclic group of that order, it generates.',
      'D. Mumford, « Picard groups of moduli problems » (1965); W. Fulton, M. Olsson, « The Picard group of M_{1,1} », Algebra & Number Theory 4 (2010), arXiv:0704.2214: Pic(M_{1,1}) = ℤ/12; M_{1,1} is a μ₂-gerbe over [M_{0,4}/𝔖₃], whose Picard group is then ℤ/6 — the n = 4 value, the case g = 1 of the formula above.',
