      'As of 2026-10-25: for n even the question is answered in print — Edidin–Hu (Michigan Math. J. 2025, Th. 1.3) give Pic[M_{0,n}/𝔖_{n−1}] = ℤ/(n − 1)(n − 2) for n ≥ 6, and n = 4 follows from Pic(M_{1,1}) = ℤ/12 (Mumford; Fulton–Olsson); the order n − 1 of L is within a few lines of Gorchinskiy–Viviani and Arsie–Vistoli. What is not found in print is the case n odd (n = 5 in the table: L_5 of order 12); it follows by the same method (with x_n = ∞, the stack is monic squarefree polynomials of degree n − 1 modulo the affine group, the discriminant has weight (n − 1)(n − 2)), which is a recomputation, not a priority claim. What would settle it: a printed computation of Pic[M_{0,n}/𝔖_{n−1}] for n odd, or the question put to a specialist (MathOverflow 516243, open).',
