    lean: { file: "lean/Grothendieck/Folder154.lean", found: "Holds in the edition's combinatorial model, more generally than stated. Positions are Las Vergnas cocircuit signatures σ : V → {−,0,+} (one representative per vertex) valid on every line, a line being a sequence of vertices with orientation signs and validity meaning + … + (0) − … − up to reversal, at most one zero, not all zero. A valid line carries at most one zero, so two vertices of D never share a line of Σ, and any sign vector agreeing with σ_D off its zeros is again a position: the choices at the ν vertices are independent. Restriction to the zeros of σ_D is a bijection from the generisations of D onto {−,0,+}^ν respecting specialisation, and these sign vectors are the faces of [−1,1]^ν ordered by reverse inclusion, the zero-free ones being its vertices; hence 3^ν generisations, 2^ν stable and ν·2^(ν−1) sub-stable. Neither ν ≥ 2 nor the arrangement axioms are used. Not formalised: topological pseudolines (Folkman–Lawrence representation), the tension with the surface X* of page 150 for ν ≥ 3, the 2ν count for straight lines, and the open question of page 153." },
