    settle:
      "Searched 2026-10-25 with WebSearch (standard and extended), WebFetch, Crossref API and pdftotext on the downloaded scan: queries on germs of clopen subsets of deleted neighbourhoods of a closed set, local ends / Stone space over A, cutting a space along a closed subset with j_*Z/2 and Stone spectrum, and Michael's « Cuts ». Found and read E. Michael, Cuts, Acta Math. 111 (1964): a general-topological, structure-free construction of X cut along a thin A (Tychonoff X), with a proper light map Ã → A whose fibres are compact totally disconnected — this is in substance the space X̃ ⊃ Ã that the folder uses on p. 16 without definition, and very probably the same Ã as the relative Stone spectrum of (j_*F_2)|_A (Example (4) gives fibre β N ∖ N, the Stone space of the stalk), though Michael never states the fibre as the Stone space of the stalk of germs. Not found anywhere read: the Boolean algebra of rives as global germs along A of clopens of V ∖ A, the sheaf-theoretic description Ã = Spec((j_*F_2)|_A), the map (*) Riv(A,X) → Comp(Ã) with injectivity in general and bijectivity for X paracompact, the bi-rives and the space Dec_β(A,X) obtained by collapsing the two halves of Ã onto A. Remains: check Fox, « Covering spaces with singularities » (1957), Sklyarenko's perfect compactifications, Freudenthal 1942 (Ann. of Math. 43), and Bredon/Johnstone as the earlier settle field asked (not opened in this pass); check whether a later paper on Michael cuts identifies the fibres of Ã → A with Stone spaces of germ algebras. Closest in print: E. Michael, Cuts, Acta Math. 111 (1964), Theorem 1.1 and §4: constructs the cut space X̃ and Ã → A for any thin subset of a Tychonoff space, with the Möbius example, by a β(X∖A) monotone-light factorisation rather than by germs or sheaves. It differs from the finding in having no Boolean algebra Riv(A,X) of global sides, no j_*F_2 / relative Stone spectrum description, no comparison map Riv(A,X) → Comp(Ã) (injective, bijective for paracompact X), and no bi-rive-based space Dec_β(A,X) contracting each half of Ã onto A; it also needs X Tychonoff and A thin, where the folder takes an arbitrary space and closed A.",
