    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder50.lean', found: "The frame is formalised at one object and one polarising class ξ, transported to End(A) by φ_ξ⁻¹ (Rosati involution as a star ring). The identities (1)–(3) of page 9, (uv)* = v*u* and ν(uv) = ν(u)ν(v) follow; ν(α + n), n ∈ ℤ, is the value of a unique monic rational polynomial of degree 2r with constant term ν(α), so the σᵢ are well defined. The trace formula tr(α)·I(ξ^r) = r·I(ξ^{r−1}, D_ξ(α)) holds when I is symmetric (tr_mul_I), and with it page 6's tr(α′α) = 2r·I(ξ^{r−1}, α*ξ)/I(ξ^r); for αα′ the axioms give α′*ξ in the last slot. Without symmetry it fails in a model of all the axioms (ℤ², I(x, y) = x₁y₂, r = 2): tr(1, 0) = 2 but the formula gives 4 or 0 depending on the slot — the pass's point (1) confirmed. The Corollaire (Rosati positivity) does not follow, even with I(ξ^{r−1}, η) > 0 for every nonzero η ∈ N⁺: in the quaternions ℍ[ℤ, 0, 0, 0] with i² = j² = 0, i ≠ 0 and tr(i′i) = 0, because i*ξ = 0. It does follow once that positivity and α ≠ 0 ⇒ α*ξ ≠ 0 are added (tr_star_mul_self_pos). Not formalised: the category itself, Propriété fondamentale 1, pages 2 and 4." },
