    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder101.lean', found: "Holds, in the page’s model (duality_dim_one, with eq_zero_of_mem, lift_K, lift_vs, baer_KA). For A a complete discrete valuation ring with fraction field K and any triple (M₀, M₁, u) — an A-module, a K-vector space and an A-linear map — the duality maps Ext⁰ → Hom_A(Coker u, K/A) and Ext¹ → Hom_A(Ker u, K/A) are bijective, Ext^• being the cohomology of Hom_K(M₁, K) → Hom_A(M₀, K/A), g ↦ g ∘ u mod A. The page’s three facts are proved: a K-linear map into A is zero; every A-linear map K → K/A is x ↦ cx mod A for some c ∈ K, the series of the page converging by completeness, so every A-linear map from a K-vector space to K/A lifts to K; and K/A is injective by Baer’s criterion. The end of the injectivity argument, partly illegible on the page and restored by the reading, checks. Completeness is used only in the lifting step. Not formalised: the equivalence between O_X-modules on Spec A and triples, and the computation of Ext and of local cohomology in that model, which are the page’s reduction; the converse (Ext¹_A(K, A) = 0 forces completeness) is not proved either. Added 2026-10-26: the converse is now proved (isAdicComplete_of_lift, isAdicComplete_iff_lift): for A a discrete valuation ring with fraction field K, A is complete if and only if every A-linear map K → K/A lifts to an A-linear map K → K, i.e. Hom_A(K, K) → Hom_A(K, K/A) is onto. A Cauchy sequence (eₙ) defines f(x) = eₙx mod A for any n with ϖⁿx ∈ A, and a lift g of f has limit g(1); Hausdorffness is Krull's theorem from Mathlib. So the reading's footnote (Ext¹_A(K, A) = 0 is equivalent to completeness) checks. Still not formalised: the identification of Ext¹_A(K, A) with that cokernel (Mathlib's categorical Ext is not used), the equivalence between O_X-modules and triples, and the computation of Ext and local cohomology in that model." },
