    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder72.lean', found: "Holds on R-points, in the coordinates (s₀, a₀, …, aₙ) over any commutative ring (any μᵢ, βᵢ): 𝒰_ρ(R) = {λ : 1 + ρλ a unit} is a commutative group under λ + λ′ + ρλλ′; λ ↦ 1 + ρλ is onto the units of every R-algebra iff ρ is a unit (forall_surjective_iff; the test algebra is the dual numbers, unit 1 + ε), and 𝒰₀ ≅ 𝔾_a (U_zero). With c̃ obtained by back-substitution and ρ = π(c̃), u_λ = id + λπ⊗c̃ satisfies u_λu_λ′ = u_{λ*λ′}, commutes with the τᵢ and has det 1 + ρλ (det_u). The page-38 isomorphism, in its linear form: an endomorphism commutes with all τᵢ iff it is c + tπ⊗c̃ with (c, t) unique (commute_iff, coeff_unique), invertible iff c and c + tρ are units (isUnit_iff), so Rˣ × 𝒰_ρ(R) ≅ Aut(E, (τᵢ)) (centraliserEquiv). D₀ = H₁ ∩ ⋯ ∩ Hₙ is {as₀ + tc̃}, and its points off c and d, normalised by ⟨s, a′₀⟩ = 1, are exactly the u_λs₀ = s₀ + λc̃, each for one λ, with u_μ(u_λs₀) = u_{λ*μ}s₀: a trivial torsor (mem_startPoints_iff, u_e0_injective, u_u_e0). For n = 1, ρ = μ₀μ₁ − β₀, 4 − β₀ for reflections, as page 41. Not formalised: the group scheme and its smoothness, the projective statement over a base (automorphisms of P(E) commuting with the projective τᵢ), the torsor of flags (page 87 C)." },
