    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder140_1.lean', found: "Proved for H¹(𝔖₃, O(U_{0,3})^*) in a model of the units, not for the Picard group of the stack. The units are modelled as k^* × λ^ℤ × (1 − λ)^ℤ with the anharmonic action, the extension 0 → k^* → O(U)^* → V(J) → 0 of the margin (checked against the substitutions evaluated at the points of U: ev_smul_lam, ev_smul_lam′, smul_incl). The bound is the reading’s: H¹(𝔖₃, V(J)) ≅ ℤ/3, H¹(𝔖₃, k^*) = μ₂(k), so the order divides 6, and 3 if 2 = 0 (card_H1_dvd, card_H1_units_dvd). The lower bound uses the tangent cocycle σ ↦ (h⁻¹)′(λ) (ev_tan): its divisor is twice the generator of H¹(𝔖₃, V(J)), so 3 divides its order, and at the transposition of 0 and 1, which fixes ∞, its constant is −1, so 2 does when 2 ≠ 0 (dvd_of_zsmul_tan). Hence, for a domain k, H¹ is ℤ/6 when 2 ≠ 0 (characteristic 3 included) and ℤ/3 when 2 = 0, generated by the tangent class (H1_units, H1_units_char_two). Not formalised: that the units of U_{0,3} are the model, Pic(U_{0,3}) = 0 and the Hochschild–Serre step identifying the Picard group of the stack with H¹, a general base S, and the page’s generator O(1) on P(V_J) — the generator here is the tangent class. Added 2026-10-25: the model is now identified with the actual units: for a domain k, the units of k[λ, 1/λ, 1/(1 − λ)] (Localization.Away (X(1 − X)) of k[X]) are exactly c λ^a (1 − λ)^b, c ∈ k^*, a, b ∈ ℤ, so O(U_{0,3})^* ≅ Units3 k with constants going to constants (unitsEquiv, toUnits_bijective, exists_unitOf, unitOf_eq_one, toUnits_incl), and Pic(U_{0,3}) = 0 over a field, U_{0,3} being a localization of the PID K[λ], hence factorial (pic_O3_subsingleton). Still not formalised: the 𝔖₃-action on k[λ, 1/λ, 1/(1 − λ)] by the anharmonic substitutions and the equivariance of unitsEquiv (only checked pointwise by ev_smul_lam), Pic(U_{0,3}) = 0 over a general base S, the Hochschild–Serre step identifying the Picard group of the stack with H¹, and the page’s generator O(1) on P(V_J)." },
