    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder1.lean', found: "Partly, in finite dimension: the cases m ≤ 2 for every n (m = 1 is Ky Fan’s inequality; m = 2 follows the page’s Λ² route written with 2×2 minors, and holds as stated) and the implication from the system to the product form, hence (15) for n ≤ 2, are proved; the cases 3 ≤ m ≤ n and compact operators are not. Added 2026-10-25: Yes, in finite dimension over ℂ, for every m and n: σ_n^m(u+v) ≤ Σ_{p≤m} σ_n^p(u) σ_n^{m−p}(v) holds as stated (sigma_system), hence the product form (15) for every n and r ≥ 0 and the subadditivity Σ_{i<n} s_i(u+v)^p ≤ Σ s_i(u)^p + Σ s_i(v)^p for 0 < p < 1, unconditionally. The proof keeps the page's Λ^m expansion, written with principal m×m minors α_m(M) = Σ_{|K|=m} det M_K, but never bounds the mixed terms (Λ^p u)∧(Λ^q v) separately: with x_j, y_j the first n Schmidt vectors of u+v, the compression (⟨y_i, w x_j⟩) of w factors as (√S_w Φ_w)*(√S_w Ψ_w) through w's Schmidt expansion, so the compression of u+v is G*H with H, G of size 2d×d; α_m(G*H) = α_m(HG*) (Sylvester), each minor obeys |det(HG*)_K|² ≤ det(HH*)_K det(GG*)_K, Fischer's inequality splits det(HH*)_K along the u and v blocks, and the constant p!q!/(p+q)! never appears. Prop. 3 is replaced by its half that is used, a Cauchy-interlacing bound α_p(Ψ*SΨ) ≤ σ_n^p(w), proved by the min-max dimension count. Not formalised: m ≥ 3 over ℝ (m ≤ 2 is), the trace-class formula (14), Prop. 3 as a supremum, compact operators on Hilbert spaces, and the optimality claim of p. 73. Added 2026-10-26: Yes, over ℝ as well: for linear maps between finite-dimensional real inner product spaces, σ_n^m(u+v) ≤ Σ_{p≤m} σ_n^p(u) σ_n^{m−p}(v) for every m and n (sigma_system_real), hence (15) for every n and the subadditivity of Σ_{i<n} s_i^p, 0 < p < 1, over ℝ. The proof complexifies: the matrix of u in orthonormal bases, read over ℂ, has u*u's characteristic polynomial mapped to ℂ, so the same singular values, and the complex theorem applies. Prop. 3 also holds as a supremum, in finite dimension over ℂ: σ_n^m(u) is the largest value of |α_m(wu)| over contractions w : F → E of rank ≤ n, attained by w₀ = Σ_{j<n} e_j⟨f_j, ·⟩ (isGreatest_norm_alpha_comp); the upper bound writes wu in the Schmidt basis of w* as a compression of u by orthogonal families of norm ≤ 1 and uses the Cauchy–Schwarz and interlacing lemmas. Still not formalised: the second form sup α_m(|wu|) of Prop. 3, Prop. 3 over ℝ, the trace-class formula (14), compact operators on Hilbert spaces, and the optimality claim of p. 73." },
