    lean: { file: 'lean/Grothendieck/Folder93.lean', found: "Holds in the abelian-group version (not sheaves): for a torsor P under an abelian group G, u : P → Hom⁰(K′, K″) and k : G → Hom⁻¹(K′, K″) additive with u(g + p) − u(p) = dk(g) + k(g)d and the u(p) morphisms of complexes, the extension Ḡ of ℤ by G with j⁻¹(1) = P is built as a quotient of G × ℤ[P] without choosing a point; [G → Ḡ] is quasi-isomorphic to ℤ (ι injective, ker j = G, j onto, e : P ≃ j⁻¹(1)); φ⁰ with φ⁰|_P = u, φ⁰ι = δk and δφ⁰ = 0 makes (k, φ⁰) a morphism of complexes into Hom•(K′, K″); the class of u(p) in the homotopy category and in D(C) does not depend on p (k(p′ − p) is the homotopy). For abelian groups this is only independence of the choice; what the pages want, no covering for a sheaf torsor without global section, is not formalised, nor the de Rham application." },
