    settle:
      'Read Knus, Quadratic and Hermitian Forms over Rings, ch. V (quaternion algebras, generalised crossed products), and Gross–Lucianovic 2009 for a description of the quaternion rings containing two given quadratic subalgebras H, H′ with H + H′ of rank 3 as a torsor under (L ⊗ L′)^∨, and for its discriminant-zero locus. Then read Voight GTM 288 chapters 22 and 30 rather than searching them by keyword. If any of them identifies that locus with Spec of the product H * H′, mark matched. This pass found it neither in Voight 2011 § 4 nor in Voight 2016, and searched GTM 288 by keyword only.',
    lean: { file: "lean/Grothendieck/Folder83.lean", found: "The algebraic core holds in coordinates over any commutative ring, characteristic 2 included, for H = k[u]/(u² − bu + c) and H′ = k[v]/(v² − b′v + c′) free (L, L′ trivialised, so (L ⊗ L′)^∨ = k). For every t the table of page 92 defines an associative unital algebra M(b, c; b′, c′; t) on P = k⁴ inducing H and H′, in which every element satisfies Hamilton–Cayley for Tr and det, with det multiplicative and Tr(uv) = t (mulM_assoc, hamilton_cayley, nrdM_mulM). Conversely, in any k-algebra whose elements satisfy Hamilton–Cayley, the relation vu = (t − bb′) + b′u + bv − uv with t = bb′ + c + c′ − N(u + v) makes x ↦ x₀ + x₁u + x₂v + x₃uv multiplicative from M(t); t is unique when this map is injective, and distinct t give distinct structures (realise_mulM, realise_unique, mulM_inj), so the structures form the affine line of t. On that line δ_{P,B}, the half discriminant of det on B = k1 + ku + kv, is −Q(t) with Q = t² − bb′t + b²c′ + b′²c − 4cc′ (deltaPB_eq); disc Q = δδ′, Q(bb′ − t) = Q(t), and the trace form of M(t) has determinant −Q² (det_traceForm). In H ⊗ H′, u * v = b′u + bv − 2u ⊗ v is a root of Q, by Q(w) = (2V − b′)²(U² − bU + c) + δ(V² − b′V + c′), giving k[t]/(Q) → H ⊗ H′ (starHom); both conjugations send u * v to bb′ − u * v; for characters (φ, φ′) into any commutative k-algebra, (φ ⊗ φ′)(u * v) = t_{φ,φ′}(u, v) = b′z + bz′ − 2zz′, a root of Q, a twist, sent to bb′ − t by conjugating φ. The reading's corrected constant term b²c′ + b′²c − 4cc′ is confirmed. Not formalised: the intrinsic torsors over a base and the chain AZ_P → … → L_P, the criterion « Azumaya iff Q invertible » of page 98 (only the trace-form determinant −Q²), and the identification S̃ ≅ X ∧ X′ as a quotient of X × X′, whose algebraic core (the invariants of σ ⊗ σ′ are k[u * v] when (2, b, b′) = 1) is Folder84's invariants_of_span_eq_top. Added 2026-10-25: the criterion « Azumaya iff Q invertible » of page 98 is now proved for Mathlib's IsAzumaya, over any commutative ring, characteristic 2 included and with no hypothesis on δ, δ′: M(b, c; b′, c′; t), made a k-algebra (MAlg), is Azumaya iff Q(t) is a unit (isAzumaya_iff), equivalently iff δ_{P,B} is a unit (isAzumaya_iff_deltaPB); over a field iff Q(t) ≠ 0, so the non-Azumaya locus of the line is exactly S̃ (isAzumaya_iff_ne_zero); and M(0, 0; 0, 0; t) is Azumaya iff t is a unit (page 97, isAzumaya_nilpotent_iff). The proof computes the matrix of M ⊗ Mᵒᵖ → End M, shows Tr(x ↦ axa′) = Tr(a)Tr(a′), and gets ± det² = Q¹⁶ from the Kronecker square of the trace form (sandwich_gram, sandwich_det_sq). Still not formalised: the intrinsic form of the criterion (two transverse rank-2 subalgebras of a locally free rank-4 algebra), the intrinsic torsors and the chain AZ_P → … → L_P, and S̃ ≅ X ∧ X′ as a quotient of X × X′." },
